This file lists the third-party components that Kupferdraht links or
compiles into its artifacts: the crates of the Cargo dependency graph
(`cargo tree -p kupferdraht-core -p kupferdraht-cli --target all
-e normal,build`; development-only dependencies such as the test HTTP
mock are left out) and the components outside that graph. The full
license texts are in docs/THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.html, generated by
cargo-about from the same graph; each crate's own copyright notice is in
the source repository linked below.

Note for application developers: the Kotlin, Swift and browser bindings
embed Kupferdraht and these components. An application that ships them
to end users must reproduce the attribution notices and license texts
the respective licenses require (the Apache-2.0 text and any NOTICE
file contents, the MIT and BSD copyright and permission notices, the
MPL-2.0 source-availability terms for the MPL-licensed crates), and
Kupferdraht's own GPL-3.0-only terms apply to the combined work.

Target scope: a crate marked "(browser target only)" ends up only in the
wasm32 build of the library, one marked "(native targets only)" only in
native builds (desktop, Android, iOS); unmarked crates are in both. A crate
used only at build time, or behind a `cfg` no build sets, is in no artifact;
its marker says at most which build uses it.
Where a crate is offered under a choice of licenses, the section says
which one Kupferdraht uses it under.

